      'Rule example: Score the most points over 4 rounds by forming melds and canastas. Be the first partnership to go out (empty hand and foot).',
      'Turn-flow example: Turn Structure: 1. Draw: Draw 2 cards from stock OR pick up entire discard pile (if you can immediately use the top card in a meld). 2. Meld: Lay down melds or add to existing partnership melds. 3. Discard: Discard 1 card to end turn. Minimum Initial Meld: Round 1: 50 points, Round 2: 90 points, Round 3: 120 points, Round 4: 150 points. Picking Up Your Foot: After playing all cards from your hand, pick up your foot. If you discard your last hand card, pick up foot on next turn. If you play all hand cards without discarding, immediately pick up foot and continue playing.',
      'Scoring example: Points for melds, canastas, cards in hand. Deductions for unmelded cards. Clean canastas worth 500, dirty canastas worth 300. Red Threes +100 if melded, -100 if caught. Game played over 4 rounds. Highest total score after 4 rounds wins. First partnership to 10,000+ points across multiple games wins the session..',
